          "links": null
        }
      ],
      "title": "Character Sheet x3",
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "0.37.0",
        "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Edit REF 1 directly. REF 1 is the target image to be modified. REF 2 is the replacement character.\n\nREPLACE EVERY GREY MANNEQUIN FIGURE VISIBLE IN REF 1 WITH THE HUMAN CHARACTER FROM REF 2.\n\nThe grey mannequin is NOT part of the background or template design. It is a placeholder character that MUST be removed and replaced.\n\nThere are THREE grey mannequin representations in REF 1 and ALL THREE must be replaced by the SAME character from REF 2:\n\n1. Replace the LARGE grey mannequin close-up on the LEFT with a LARGE close-up of the character from REF 2. The character's head, face, hair, neck, shoulders and upper torso must occupy the same large area as the grey mannequin currently occupies. Preserve the mannequin's existing crop, scale, framing and position.\n\n2. Replace the FRONT-FACING full-body grey mannequin in the CENTRE with a full-body front view of the character from REF 2. Preserve its existing position, scale, pose and framing.\n\n3. Replace the SIDE-PROFILE full-body grey mannequin on the RIGHT with a side-profile view of the SAME character from REF 2. Preserve its existing position, scale, pose, orientation and framing.\n\nREF 2 is the ONLY source for character identity and appearance. Preserve the character's face, hairstyle, hair colour, body proportions, clothing, footwear and other visible details consistently across all three replacements.\n\nFor the side profile, infer the character's corresponding side appearance naturally from REF 2 while maintaining the same identity and clothing.\n\nCRITICAL EDIT REQUIREMENTS:\n\nREMOVE AND REPLACE EVERY GREY MANNEQUIN.\nZERO GREY MANNEQUINS may remain in the final image.\nThe large grey mannequin close-up on the left MUST NOT remain.\nDo not treat the large grey mannequin as background artwork.\nDo not preserve the mannequin's grey head, face, skin or body.\nDo not place the new character beside or over the mannequin while leaving the mannequin visible.\n\nPreserve REF 1's exact layout.\nPreserve the exact white background.\nPreserve the relative size and position of all three existing figures.\nDo not redesign the character sheet.\nDo not create a new layout.\nDo not add additional people or views.\nDo not make all three character representations the same size.\n\nThis is an IN-PLACE CHARACTER REPLACEMENT of REF 1:\nGREY MANNEQUIN = REMOVE.\nCHARACTER FROM REF 2 = REPLACE IT.\n\nFinal result: exactly THREE representations of the character from REF 2 and ZERO representations of the grey mannequin."
      ]
    },
